      "text": {
        "source": "const fs = require(\"node:fs\");\n\nfunction configReaderReadConfig(path) {\n  const stat = fs.statSync(path);\n  if (!stat.isFile()) throw new Error(`Configuration path is not a regular file: ${path}`);\n  return fs.readFileSync(path, \"utf8\");\n}",
        "specification": "Service library that reads the complete content of a caller-supplied file path and returns it as text. It must distinguish an empty file from a read failure, close resources deterministically, preserve UTF-8 content, reject directories, and report the path in errors without exposing unrelated filesystem data. Parsing JSON, YAML, properties, or another configuration syntax belongs to the caller.",
        "aiInstructions": "Expose a small `read_config(path)`-style API in the effective language. Return file text; do not silently parse or substitute defaults."
      }
    }
  ]
}
